        ~5 minutes with the commands under HOW TO RE-RUN.

=================== WHY THIS MEASUREMENT ===================

perf_2026-09-05-lilith1-POSITION priced the inter frame by differencing
wall-clock medians (frames=2 minus frames=1): gradient 512 p8 port 18.16 ms
vs C 3.78 ms, photo_cid 512 p6 port 22.23 ms vs C 3.76 ms — roughly 4-6x on
the inter frame against 1.6-2.4x whole-sequence ratios. Its own record says
C's side is unresolved: C's p25/p75 spreads are the size of the difference.
Callgrind is deterministic, so the same N=2 - N=1 subtraction on instruction
counts is exact on BOTH sides and resolves per function. Reading rule for
everything below: a function present in both cells with the same count
reads 0 (frame-0 work, setup and teardown cancel); what remains is what the
second, INTER frame added, plus any frame-0 work whose cost changed because
a second frame exists. The per-function self deltas sum to the process
delta EXACTLY on every one of the six runs (inter_delta.py checks it).

=================== BYTE-IDENTITY (all six cells, both frames) ===================

Per FRAME, never on the concatenation (a frame-0 length change would shift
every later byte): port <pfx>.obu.f<i> vs C <pfx>.c.obu.pts<i>.

  cell            N  port Ir          C Ir           ident      cg-run ident
  gradient p8   vk  934,458,067     416,659,007    f0=Y       port Y / C Y
  gradient p8   n2  1,365,365,445   473,339,517    f0=Y,f1=Y  port Y / C Y
  gradient p6   vk  2,186,794,627   904,932,961    f0=Y       port Y / C Y
  gradient p6   n2  3,164,727,585   1,036,023,248  f0=Y,f1=Y  port Y / C Y
  photo_cid p6  vk  4,033,992,400   2,095,904,172  f0=Y       port Y / C Y
  photo_cid p6  n2  4,700,316,832   2,225,469,006  f0=Y,f1=Y  port Y / C Y

"cg-run ident" = the OBU the callgrind-instrumented run itself wrote, cmp'd
against the un-instrumented pre-pass's. The p2 inter cells the brief warned
about (ident=N) were not run.

=================== THE ARM EACH SIDE ENTERED UNDER VALGRIND ===================

Verified from the profiles, not assumed. Valgrind masks the AVX-512 CPUID
bits, and BOTH sides fell back symmetrically:
  port: the binary carries two `_v4` symbols (svtav1_dsp::restoration::
        __arcane_wiener_convolve_simd_v4 and its closure, from 373243b7);
        the N=2 profiles contain ZERO rows naming a `_v4`/`_v4x` symbol and
        36 (gradient p8) / 37 (photo p6) rows naming `_v3` (AVX2-class)
        symbols. No `_neon`/`_scalar` rows.
  C:    the binary carries 180 `*avx512*` symbols (nm); the N=2 profiles
        contain ZERO rows naming an avx512 symbol and 115 / 123 rows naming
        `_avx2` symbols (plus 25-38 `_sse*`).
So every number here prices the port's `_v3` arm against C's AVX2 arm. That
is the like-for-like the brief required. It also means the C oracle's real
AVX-512 kernels (which it DOES run on r7900x/lilith hardware) are priced at
their AVX2 cost here — a caveat that cuts AGAINST the port on hardware.

=================== THE POSITION: WHOLE-PROCESS INTER DELTA ===================

  cell            port delta     C delta       port/C   encoder-only*  ratio*
  gradient 512 p8  430,907,378   56,680,510    7.60x    424,211,295    7.48x
  gradient 512 p6  977,932,958  131,090,287    7.46x    971,236,875    7.41x
  photo_cid 512 p6 666,324,432  129,564,834    5.14x    659,628,349    5.09x

  * minus `perf_encode::translate` (6,696,083 Ir, 3 calls): the PORT harness
    synthesises the shifted frame in-process; the C driver reads it from the
    .yuv (an fread). Harness work, excluded from every encoder reading.

The wall-clock differencing said "4-6x"; the instruction count says 5.1-7.6x.
Ir is not wall clock (the port's IPC is above C's per stall_attrib_2026-09-05,
and callgrind overstates zero-fills ~10x), so the two are consistent, and
neither number should be converted into the other.

