gradient 512x512 p6 (port 977.9 M, C 131.1 M) — the two things p8 could not show

  DIRECTIONAL INTRA on the inter frame is the #1 row: 265,516,912 (27.2 %) vs
  C 14,183,841 (18.7x self). dr_z2_edged_core alone 157,368,694 (16.1 %) vs C
  z2 11,316,804 (13.9x). The key-frame counts are EXACT joins (port
  dr_predictor_edged 40,758 = C z1+z2+z3 13,746+20,288+6,724; z2 20,288 =
  20,288), so the inter-frame deltas are real: the port runs +4,346
  directional predictions where C runs +1,965, and +2,288 z2 where C runs
  +1,053 — 2.2x the BREADTH on top of the per-call kernel gap (~10x per z2
  call, approximate because the block-size mix may differ). The kernel gap is
  the one 1d9e5069f's "generic magetypes route" note already names; the
  breadth is new and inter-frame-specific: on the KEY frame the two sides
  inject the same directional set, on the INTER frame the port injects ~2.2x
  C's. Which C gate the port lacks was not traced.
  MDS0 VAR distortion: 97,165,776 (9.9 %) vs C 7,291,250 (13.3x) at +6,032 vs
  +10,157 calls — variance_diff_parts_impl_v3 costs ~16 k Ir per call against
  C's variance32x32/64x64 at ~0.7-2 k. It is the port's single largest kernel
  in the whole photo N=2 run (350.8 M self, 7.46 % of the run). sse_madd_
  2026-09-05 fixed variance::sse; THIS kernel (variance_diff_parts) is a
  different one and is untouched.
  ME family: block_sad 127,945,680 (13.1 %), ext_all8 402 = 402, sad_loop
  640 = 640, 52.1x / 48.4x per call — identical shape to p8.
  Leaves: evaluate_leaf +208 vs md_encode_block +300 — the count join that is
  exact at p8 and on the key frame BREAKS on the p6 inter frame: the port
  evaluates FEWER leaves (and on photo p6, 64 vs 320 — one per SB). See OPEN.

photo_cid 512x512 p6 (port 666.3 M, C 129.6 M, 5.14x)

  ME family 25.1 % (block_sad 167,061,918; ME whole 170,144,888 vs 4,866,029 =
  35.0x at 64 = 64; ext_all8 762 = 762 at 52.1x; sad_loop 640 = 640 at 48.6x)
  and directional intra 26.9 % (178,981,848 vs 15,571,681, 11.5x) are more
  than half of the port's inter delta between them. Then variance_diff 7.8 %
  (6.3x), memset 5.7 % (suspect), Hadamard 4.6 % (C 0), MD inter prediction
  24,012,172 vs 12,457,707 (1.9x — but at 256 vs 2,284 calls, so per call
  ~17x), subpel 19,634,176 vs 10,854,294 (1.8x at 128 vs 640 calls).
  On this cell the port's MD BREADTH is far below C's: predict_unit +1,856
  vs fast_loop_core +6,484, leaves +64 vs +320, subpel 128 vs 640, inter
  predictions 256 vs 2,284 — and the bytes are identical. The 5.1x is
  therefore entirely per-call cost on a NARROWER search; per unit of MD work
  the port is further from C here than the headline ratio says.

=================== ALGORITHMIC vs PER-CALL — THE VERDICT ===================

PER-CALL (same or near-same call count both sides, the fix is a kernel):
  * the open-loop ME SAD family — the largest item on every cell (22-25 % of
    the port's inter delta at 30-35x C for motion_estimation_b64 at 64 = 64
    calls). C's svt_ext_all_sad_calculation_8x8_16x16_avx2 computes all
    8x8 SADs of a 16x16 region and sums them in one pass (2.8 k Ir per call);
    the port's dispatch loops block_sad 512 times per call (148 k Ir). Same
    for sad_loop_kernel (1.2 k vs 52 k per call). This is a kernel-shape gap,
    not a search-breadth gap: the search visits the same points.
  * the inter-prediction convolves (x 125x, 2-D 217x, y 15x per call — the
    port's port_convolve::* is scalar) plus the routing defect that sends
    y-only-subpel blocks through the 2-pass path.
  * subpel variance (4.7x), build_nmv_component_cost_table (3.5x at 4 = 4),
    downsample_2d (23.6x at 2 = 2), variance_diff (the MDS0 VAR kernel, ~10x
    per call), the directional-intra kernels (~10x per call), PD0 whole SB
    (4.1x at 64 = 64), PD0 inter prediction (45x at 320 = 320).

ALGORITHMIC (the port does work C does not do on this frame — the fix is
wiring, and each is byte-inert by construction):
  * MDS0 Hadamard SATD on inter candidates (33.6 M / 50.4 M / 30.4 M; C 0)
  * the screen-content detector, twice per frame on every frame (19.1 M; C 0)
  * the homegrown motion_est::full_pel_search per SB (16.8 M; C 0)
  * film-grain estimate with a discarded result (3.4 M/frame; C 0)
  * tpl_sb_qp_offsets with a discarded result (2.3 M/frame; C 0)
  * allocator traffic (+31.7 k calls on the inter frame vs C +17)
  * directional-intra BREADTH on the inter frame (+4,346 vs +1,965 at p6)
  Summed for gradient p8 (Hadamard 33.6 + sc detector 19.1 + full_pel_search
  16.8 + allocator 4.7 + film grain 3.4 + tpl offsets 2.3): ~80 M of the
  port's 424 M encoder delta (19 %) is work C does not do at all; the other
  ~81 % is per-call.

C DOES WORK THE PORT DOES NOT (the port's delta is UNDERSTATED by these):
  * warped-motion candidates: svt_av1_warp_plane 287 / 318 calls at p6
    (8.8 M / 9.9 M Ir); the port has no warp arm (CONTEXT-HANDOFF §6 names
    it as the next inter blocker). Bytes match because no warp candidate won
    on these cells.
  * the Wiener LR search on the inter frame: C's restoration_seg_search 1 -> 2,
    search_wiener_seg 4 -> 8, compute_stats 4 -> 8 (5.4 M / 5.4 M / 5.0 M
    incl); the port's search_restoration_still_bd stays 1 -> 1 and its
    compute_stats 4 -> 4. C's is_not_last_layer = !is_highest_layer, and
    is_highest_layer is `(tl == hier) && hier != 0` (pd_process.c:5560), so on
    this flat GOP wn_filter_lvl = 5 at <= M8 and C searches; the port derives
    the same flag (pipeline.rs:5092-5095, port_picstruct::is_highest_layer)
    yet ran no search on the inter frame. Byte-identical here only because
    C signalled RESTORE_NONE. THIS IS A BYTE HAZARD for the inter campaign on
    content where C's inter-frame Wiener search finds a filter — flagged, not
    diagnosed.
  * MD breadth at p6: C evaluates more leaves (300 vs 208; photo 320 vs 64)
    and more MDS0 candidates (6,484 vs 1,856 on photo). Either C's depth
    refinement admits sub-depths the port's never does, or C's extra
    md_encode_block calls exit early — not resolved here; a byte hazard of
    the same kind if a child depth ever wins in C.

=================== TRAPS PAID FOR, AND HOW TO READ THE TABLE ===================

  * `evaluate_leaf` read 64 vs md_encode_block 320 on photo before recursion
    clones were folded: callgrind names recursion levels `fn'2`, and a
    `$`-anchored regex saw only level 1. inter_join.py folds them. The count
    is STILL 64 vs 320 after folding — that one is real (above).
  * The PD0 light-quant row is a COUNT control only (+320 both sides); its
    33.8x Ir is the scope trap the brief named — C's quantize_inv_quantize_
    light excludes the transform the port's tx_quant_core includes.
  * memset's largest port caller is the allocator's unnamed frame
    (0x4cf4730, 10,471 calls / 42.3 M): calloc zero-fill counted under memset
    AND under the allocator. Both rows are flagged; neither is a wall-clock
    prediction.
  * The "MD inter prediction whole" join is by call-graph position; C's
    svt_aom_inter_prediction is per (block, plane-set) and the port's
    av1_inter_prediction_light_pd1 per block, so the ratio is honest only on
    Ir, not on the calls column.
  * Wall clock: NOT measured in this chunk and NOT derivable from it. The
    only host with counters (r7900x) was under another lane's timed bench
    from ~21:40 UTC; a `perf stat` cycles cross-check is owed when it clears.

=================== HOST CONTENTION (recorded, not a caveat on the numbers) ===================

The twelve callgrind runs completed 21:29-21:33 UTC. At ~21:40 the
coordinator reported a sibling lane's TIMED kernel bench live on r7900x
(marker `~/work/zen/zenav1-svt--v4x2/.workongoing`); no valgrind, build or
wall-clock work ran on r7900x after that — only python over the text
profiles. Callgrind counts are load-invariant, so nothing here was affected;
the other lane's wall clock during 21:29-21:33 may have been.

=================== TOOLING (new, reusable) ===================

  tools/perf_profile/callcount_cells.sh  now takes FRAMES / VIDEO / SHIFT and
        checks identity PER FRAME; writes self_*.txt and incl_*.txt at
        --threshold=100 (the default drops everything under the 99 % mark —
        exactly the small kernels a difference needs).
  tools/perf_profile/inter_delta.py      N=2 minus N=1 per symbol (self, incl,
        calls), verifies the self deltas sum to the process delta.
  tools/perf_profile/inter_join.py       the C-edge -> port-edge table (41
        edges, regex-joined by C-comment citation + call-graph position,
        every matched symbol listed), with the class each row is read as.

=================== HOW TO RE-RUN ===================

  export PATH="$HOME/.cargo/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"; cd ~/work/zen/zenav1-svt/rust
  ~/work/zen/scripts/run-heavy --jobs 8 -- env -u RUSTFLAGS cargo build --release -p zenav1-svt --example perf_encode --example identity_run
  ~/work/zen/scripts/run-heavy --jobs 8 -- tools/perf_c_encode/build.sh
  ./target/release/examples/identity_run crop:$HOME/work/codec-corpus/CID22/CID22-512/training/3571065.png 512 512 40 8 ~/tmp/cg-inter/yuv/photo_cid   # sha256 88142a48...
  O=~/tmp/cg-inter/cells; Y=~/tmp/cg-inter/yuv/photo_cid.yuv
  PRESETS="6 8" VIDEO=1 FRAMES=1 tools/perf_profile/callcount_cells.sh $O gradient_vk:gradient:512:512
  PRESETS="6"   VIDEO=1 FRAMES=1 tools/perf_profile/callcount_cells.sh $O photo_vk:raw:$Y:512:512
  PRESETS="6 8"         FRAMES=2 tools/perf_profile/callcount_cells.sh $O gradient_n2:gradient:512:512
  PRESETS="6"           FRAMES=2 tools/perf_profile/callcount_cells.sh $O photo_n2:raw:$Y:512:512
  for c in "gradient 8" "gradient 6" "photo 6"; do set -- $c; for s in port c; do
    python3 tools/perf_profile/inter_delta.py $O --n1 ${1}_vk --n2 ${1}_n2 --preset $2 --side $s --tsv ~/tmp/cg-inter/delta_${s}_${1}_p$2.tsv; done; done
  python3 tools/perf_profile/inter_join.py ~/tmp/cg-inter --cells gradient_p8,gradient_p6,photo_p6 --tsv join_inter.tsv
  Arm check: grep -cE "_v4x?(\s|$|::|\[)" $O/self_port_*_n2_*.txt must be 0 and grep -ci avx512 $O/self_c_*_n2_*.txt must be 0.

